comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-16T16:58:04.452Z",codex-root,Baseline lock resolves 41 advisories including critical Vitest and multiple runtime transitive highs.
  "2026-07-16T17:02:52.811Z",codex-root,"Zero-vulnerability result achieved with direct upgrades plus narrow compatible-major overrides for vulnerable MCP/Vitest transitive packages. Bun frozen install, npm resolution, TypeScript 7 check, Prettier 3.9, esbuild build, and all 614 unit tests pass."
  "2026-07-16T17:24:09.357Z",codex-root,bun outdated reports only @types/node 26 as a latest-major option; the project intentionally retains @types/node 22.20.1 to type-check against its minimum supported Node 22.12 runtime.
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-16T16:58:04.452Z",codex-root,Upgrade coupled packages together and validate majors through the full suite.
learnings[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-16T16:58:04.452Z",codex-root,Dependabot single-package updates fail frozen-lock and peer dependency checks.
  "2026-07-16T17:02:53.425Z",codex-root,Bun retained vulnerable transitive versions allowed by dependency ranges after direct upgrades; explicit patched-version overrides were required to make the resolved graph audit-clean.
  "2026-07-16T17:24:09.357Z",codex-root,"A higher @types/node major would silently permit APIs unavailable at the declared minimum runtime, so minimum-runtime alignment is intentional rather than stale dependency debt."
